as a usable private key and the engine can sign."},"2396":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Try **Sign / Verify** in KMS; check provider permissions and availability."},"2397":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"CSR"},"2398":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Correct PEM and verifiable signature."},"2399":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"`openssl req -in request.csr -noout -verify -text`."},"2400":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Profile"},"2401":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Selected source, existing ID, allowed algorithm and size."},"2402":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Check Profiles precedence; CA and DMS resolve differently."},"2403":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Result"},"2404":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Appropriate subject, SAN, usages and dates."},"2405":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Compare CSR, profile and certificate; successful issuance does not establish consumer acceptance."},"2406":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"For unexpected certificate fields, review `Honor Subject`, `Honor Key Usage`, `Honor Extended Key Usages` and `Honor Extensions`. The latter preserves SAN only, without validating entitlement to those names. Validity is not automatically clamped to CA expiration."},"2407":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"For CA reissuance failures, check revocation and date: reissuance is not supported for a revoked or already expired CA. To change its key, use Hierarchy and rotation."},"2408":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting#ocsp-or-crl-do-not-reflect-a-change","content":"Check each boundary independently:"},"2409":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting#ocsp-or-crl-do-not-reflect-a-change","content":"**Record:** read the correct certificate again by serial and issuer. Confirm status, reason and time; expired or permanently revoked records reject further transitions."},"2410":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting#ocsp-or-crl-do-not-reflect-a-change","content":"**Endpoint:** inspect AIA and CDP. Query those URLs from the consumer’s network; an old route or incorrect issuer can explain a discrepancy."},"2411":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting#ocsp-or-crl-do-not-reflect-a-change","content":"**OCSP:** save a fresh response, verify signature and timestamps, and observe status. An HTTP error for an absent serial does not mean `Good` or guarantee a signed `Unknown`."},"2412":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting#ocsp-or-crl-do-not-reflect-a-change","content":"**CRL:** compare `latest_crl`, number and timestamps with the downloaded list. Check the serial in its contents. If unchanged, review `regenerate_on_revoke`, event delivery, jobs, signing and storage with the deployment operator."},"2413":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting#ocsp-or-crl-do-not-reflect-a-change","content":"**Client:** check cache, policy for expired or unavailable evidence, critical IDP extension and rejection of a new connection."},"2414":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting#ocsp-or-crl-do-not-reflect-a-change","content":"Reactivation from `CertificateHold` needs a new CRL for the client to stop seeing the hold. Reactivating a CA does not restore its descendant cascade; inspect every status and individual operation failure."},"2415":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting#the-chain-validates-but-the-connection-fails","content":"Check expected identity, SAN, KU/EKU, matching key, presented intermediates and consumer permissions. Distinguish server TLS trust, client authentication and action authorization. Follow Validation for positive and rejection tests."},"2416":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/platform/pki/troubleshooting#the-chain-validates-but-the-connection-fails","content":"When escalating a problem, provide identifiers, error and relevant public evidence, including query timestamps and version. This distinguishes issuance, publication and consumer application failures."},"2417":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","type":"page","content":"3.8.0 to 4.0.0","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Up